<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pedro Albizu Campos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1891–1965</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pedro Albizu Campos was a Puerto Rican lawyer who became president of the Nationalist Party in 1930 and led the movement for independence from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. A Harvard law graduate, he was imprisoned for seditious conspiracy in 1936 and again after the Nationalist uprisings of 1950. He spent much of his later life in prison and died in 1965.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pedro-albizu-campos.jpg" alt="Pedro Albizu Campos" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pedro_Albizu_Campos_in_uniform.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
